      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc",
        "2": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc",
        "3": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc",
        "4": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc",
        "5": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "security-lake-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A network change happens just before traffic spikes. Were they related? Amazon Security Lake collects security evidence in one place, so your team can investigate both events together.",
          "text_sha256": "f3784894cdbb19659dab47f0d6191e57bb6d2b2307cdd8da8911c99a44ff781b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f3784894cdbb19659dab47f0d6191e57bb6d2b2307cdd8da8911c99a44ff781b",
          "asset_sha256": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc"
        },
        {
          "id": "security-lake-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Start with two sources. CloudTrail management events tell you who called an A W S A P I and what changed. V P C Flow Logs summarize network traffic, including addresses, ports, and whether traffic was accepted or rejected.",
          "text_sha256": "92681ddfd1f726a8dd385fcb6ccccf7988418748ddd9c758cd48b76bde41a2b1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "84a317056325c51eb3b56b9c77da286f5c12fe2192718b192e736b6de043f276",
          "asset_sha256": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc"
        },
        {
          "id": "security-lake-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Security Lake converts supported native A W S logs to the Open Cybersecurity Schema Framework. It stores the normalized data as par-kay files in an Amazon S three bucket in your account.",
          "text_sha256": "ebbf0aff60a39546cb665599bce7983a1f270c5d7789c50dfc5ea5608eca03b1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2743d24dc5e562e206a7b9c06741fa3436667377a4d172f7527aae5d701bc773",
          "asset_sha256": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc"
        },
        {
          "id": "security-lake-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "An analyst with permission can use Athena to compare when the change occurred with network activity. A match gives you a lead, not proof of what caused the traffic.",
          "text_sha256": "70c0df249077ad1ecc7ae48f527ae9c9b2a13c0206bfba1a53ef566310e21218",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "70c0df249077ad1ecc7ae48f527ae9c9b2a13c0206bfba1a53ef566310e21218",
          "asset_sha256": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc"
        },
        {
          "id": "security-lake-05",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "Remember the difference: Security Lake stores evidence you can query. GuardDuty analyzes signals to detect potential threats and raise findings. They work together, but they do different jobs.",
          "text_sha256": "48efe3fa8b82f628e9b5efa88a620b37a983cba82427caa8c4c8f0a9d84720a2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "48efe3fa8b82f628e9b5efa88a620b37a983cba82427caa8c4c8f0a9d84720a2",
          "asset_sha256": "6981f7c255c40135fbfc72f5e118d4eb637c147c09dfe753ccf6a94fe930e5bc"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "97",
      "revision": "m09p97-sap-intro-wave1-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810",
        "2": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810",
        "3": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810",
        "4": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810",
        "5": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "iam-identity-center-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "An engineer and an application both need A W S access, but they take different routes. I A M governs what identities can do. I A M Identity Center gives people one place to sign in to assigned accounts.",
          "text_sha256": "c815830d80390c532e8a6957e66b9cfc1f8f9d734e5ccdf4f8e7fad8fd195743",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "cf92df80692b4c1a3d30379b958026c118187730b26ef9afa98a874c6f70657b",
          "asset_sha256": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810"
        },
        {
          "id": "iam-identity-center-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Picture an engineer opening the workforce access portal. They choose the account and a role assigned to them. A permission set defines what that role allows. Access is temporary.",
          "text_sha256": "0960210f051cd52695a482494a8880447bbd963ccb1d749d91150198413fd29c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0960210f051cd52695a482494a8880447bbd963ccb1d749d91150198413fd29c",
          "asset_sha256": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810"
        },
        {
          "id": "iam-identity-center-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Lambda assumes its execution role and gets temporary credentials. If the role is authorized to read that S three object, the function can retrieve it without a workforce sign-in.",
          "text_sha256": "287fea43b143ba659eb2affaf5182fc90f50ee180c2977a4190ada806608b85b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1ec449d8ce912f702ea46a854a30475a31bbe455b6e6b699b178c8f86948eb5e",
          "asset_sha256": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810"
        },
        {
          "id": "iam-identity-center-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Here is how the two connect. Identity Center provisions an I A M role in the target account for each assigned permission set. I A M enforces the permissions when people use the role.",
          "text_sha256": "7a48fc55b0d9f8c74ac6222d57aeb93cb100daf43019c95d13edcc7df7d15773",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2b4344758af46d7abc746ed74aef063a1bc0736f528c5c2ea5835c76335e9af6",
          "asset_sha256": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810"
        },
        {
          "id": "iam-identity-center-05",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "So choose Identity Center for workforce access across accounts. Give an A W S workload a scoped I A M execution role. In both cases, grant only the permissions the work actually needs.",
          "text_sha256": "498274b750b9ea6f866a729dabf81e6113fbcc532fec37be8cecd9ee9a121c99",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d80cc2bf3026c4d0695f48c6796c835f692a26864dcb3590ebf56bf4f56fdb9d",
          "asset_sha256": "2528946a28443159570c450117eb2f4f2c586b3e32cb30dcef1e772ed9b67810"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "98",
      "revision": "m09p98-sap-intro-wave1-andrew-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b",
        "2": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b",
        "3": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b",
        "4": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b",
        "5": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "kms-secrets-manager-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Protecting a document and rotating a database password are two jobs. A W S Key Management Service, or K M S, manages cryptographic keys. Secrets Manager stores and manages secret values.",
          "text_sha256": "594d1459a2548470745af715d03dbe09d1f09bf42df4394665aa315eaddbee6f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "70a96900bcea5efd66c819e84efdf1d57d29e742230d690c12e6b8fe09c145b5",
          "asset_sha256": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b"
        },
        {
          "id": "kms-secrets-manager-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A K M S key can protect the data key that encrypts the document. The application requests an authorized cryptographic operation; it does not load the K M S key as a password.",
          "text_sha256": "e7a3c104167d98b7a8a3a52474619aec37726268e35f2c23456c72317f4f4ab6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f87259c6bb31f1a820968ed0879bb72b87dc5f7d3d41aaaf81999441fce7fc63",
          "asset_sha256": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b"
        },
        {
          "id": "kms-secrets-manager-03",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Now look at the database. The application asks Secrets Manager for the current password and uses that value to connect. When rotation is configured, Secrets Manager can update the credential and the stored secret.",
          "text_sha256": "659a5030b7d036e309dac291132380bf013e67848ee74821ebbb1f21dce5adbb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "659a5030b7d036e309dac291132380bf013e67848ee74821ebbb1f21dce5adbb",
          "asset_sha256": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b"
        },
        {
          "id": "kms-secrets-manager-04",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Secrets Manager uses a K M S key to protect the secret at rest. The application needs permission to read the secret and, for a customer managed key, permission to decrypt.",
          "text_sha256": "8b31bacb0d76e0a8c5c48ca7428f4493c88b8b3d43371bff0842395e2b04b39b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dd455ce2ba11cbf5b0b6494b5b4c61bc6968f3db5a4b9aec5632854dda4e0735",
          "asset_sha256": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b"
        },
        {
          "id": "kms-secrets-manager-05",
          "slide": 5,
          "text": "The decision is simple: use K M S to control cryptographic keys and use Secrets Manager to retrieve and rotate secrets. Protecting a password with encryption does not rotate it.",
          "text_sha256": "3a654a3c37d07d6a5148587f7b0ee938ea8ffd9b6afe5231805cbebac1581a94",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "316cdf60de88480b3062f6dc11716db045924586186e000e1b0c7a317327522b",
          "asset_sha256": "45d69af11531651ff5ea716ab18d25ca63c217d53e4333f091632b28078c673b"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
